// EXPECT-DIAG: E108
// EXPECT-DIAG: Expected a function name after 'fn'
// EXPECT-NO-DIAG: Statements are not allowed outside of a function
// LEC-005: a syntax error INSIDE a function body (here a lambda attempt --
// `fn(...)` where an expression belongs) must resynchronise at that
// function's closing brace. SkipToNextTopLevelBoundary() used to reset its
// nesting counter to 0, so recovery stopped at the next `;` still inside the
// body; the rest of the body then parsed as top-level statements and drew a
// false "Statements are not allowed outside of a function" -- usually printed
// BEFORE the real error, because that message is written directly to stderr.
fn main(): int {
    mut x: int = 1;
    mut f = fn(a: int): int { return a; };
    x = x + 1;
    return x;
}
